      en: "Željin (also known as the Raška Mountain) is a peak in central Serbia, rising to 1787 m. It lies between the Ibar and Raška rivers. Part of the Kopaonik massif, it is primarily composed of serpentinite and dunite. Vegetation includes coniferous forests (spruce, fir) and alpine meadows. It hosts rare bird species such as golden eagle. The economy involves livestock grazing and tourism. Nearby are the Studenica and Sopocani monasteries, UNESCO World Heritage sites. The mountain is popular for hiking and botanical excursions.",
